  "caption": "Quinn's elbow was fine. The shoulder, back, hip and calf? They had opinions.\n\nTennis loads far more than the elbow. The serve is a whole-body chain, and when energy leaks from legs, hips or trunk, the shoulder or low back can end up absorbing it. Sudden jumps in playing load are often part of the story.\n\nWhat often helps: build serve volume and new spins gradually, strengthen the rotator cuff and shoulder blade rather than only stretching, turn through your upper back and hips, and train calves, balance and change of direction.\n\nA sudden painful, swelling calf needs a same-day review, as does back pain with numbness or leg weakness. Shoulder pain during the serve is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
